  <text xml:lang="ta" type="edition" corresp="#Ed">
    <body>
      <div type="mūlam" rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="TNV9">
      <l>niṟaittē ṉaḻittalu neṟicceṉ ṟalaittalu</l>
<l>morukkiṉa mōmpalu muḻavoṭu payiṟalun</l>
<l>tiraikkaṭaṟ cēṟalō ṭiṉaiyaṉa ceyalē.<anchor xml:id="ceyal"/></l>
</lg>
<lg xml:lang="en">
  <l>Destroying full honeycombs, going on the road and harassing [travellers],</l> 
  <l>tending to gathered herds, practising ploughing,</l> 
<l>and going on the wavy sea – such things are the occupations.</l></lg>
</div>
</body>
</text>
<text xml:lang="ta" type="edition" corresp="#Ed">
    <body>
      <head xml:lang="en">Commentary</head>
      <div type="commentary" rend="parallel">
      <p xml:id="TNV9comm1">eṉpatu ceyti yām āṟuṇarttutaṉutaliṟṟu.</p>
      <p xml:lang="en">The quoted [<term xml:lang="ta-Latn"><hi rend="italic">cūttiram</hi></term>] intends to make known the way in which the occupations occur.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="commentary" rend="parallel">
      <p xml:id="TNV9comm2">tēṉ aḻittalum āṟalaittalunirai mēyttalum 
      uḻutaluṅ kaṭal ūṭu pukutalum eṉṟip peṟṟi yellām āṇṭaic ceytiyām eṉṟa vāṟu.</p>
      <p xml:lang="en">Destroying honeycombs, harassing [travellers] on the road, grazing herds, 
      ploughing, and entering into the sea – all [of these] are the occupations of each place in this order.<note place="foot" xml:lang="en"><q xml:lang="ta-Latn"><hi rend="italic">i peṟṟi</hi></q> performs a similar function to <q xml:lang="ta-Latn"><hi rend="italic">muṟaiyāṉē</hi></q> in previous <term xml:lang="ta-Latn"><hi rend="italic">cūttiram</hi></term>-s, as I understand it. One could also take <q xml:lang="ta-Latn"><hi rend="italic">peṟṟi</hi></q> as ‘nature’ or ‘manner’, in which case one would translate: ‘everything of such a nature…’ or ‘all of these methods…’.</note></p>
      </div>
      <div type="commentary" rend="parallel">
      <p xml:id="TNV9comm3">iṉaiyaṉa<anchor xml:id="inaiyana"/> veṉṟataṉāṟ ṟiṉai yaritaluṅ kiḻaṅkakaḻtalum<anchor xml:id="kilankakal"/> ūr 
      eṟitalunirai kōṭalum<anchor xml:id="niraikotal"/> varakaritalum ēṟu kōṭalum<anchor xml:id="erukotal"/> viḻavayartalum puṉal āṭalum<anchor xml:id="atal"/> uppākkutalumuttuk 
      kuḷittalum<anchor xml:id="kulittal"/> uḷḷiṭṭaṉa vellāṅ koḷka.<num> 9.</num></p>
      <p xml:lang="en">By <q xml:lang="ta-Latn"><hi rend="italic">iṉaiyaṉa</hi></q>, understand that all 
        [of these] are included: harvesting foxtail millet and digging up root vegetables; raiding villages and seizing 
        cattle-herds; harvesting common millet and seizing bulls; performing ceremonies and playing in the flood; 
         making salt and diving for pearls.</p>
        </div>
      </body>
      </text>
