<standOff type="notes4" corresp="#TNV9"><note xml:lang="en" target="#ceyal">The situation here is a bit odd. The occupations listed in the <term xml:lang="ta-Latn"><hi rend="italic">cūttiram</hi></term> correspond to those listed in the IAC. However, with the exception of <q xml:lang="ta-Latn"><hi rend="italic">tēṉ aḻittal</hi></q>, they are described in different wording. The IAC also lists multiple occupations per poetic setting, whereas the TNV <term xml:lang="ta-Latn"><hi rend="italic">cūttiram</hi></term> lists only one. The IAC’s occupations are provided in the notes for the commentary to avoid repetition.</note></standOff>
