<standOff type="notes1" corresp="#TNV9comm3"><note xml:lang="ta" target="#kilankakal"><term xml:lang="en">Cf. IAC1, p. 25:</term> kuṟiñcikku… ceyti tēṉaḻittaluṅ kiḻaṅkakaḻtaluṅ kuṉṟamāṭutalun tiṉaikkiḷikaṭitalum</note>
<note xml:lang="ta" target="#niraikotal"><term xml:lang="en">Cf. IAC1, p. 26:</term> pālaikku… ceyti niraikōṭaluñ cātteṟitaluñ cūṟaiyāṭalum</note>
<note xml:lang="ta" target="#erukotal"><term xml:lang="en">Cf. IAC1, p. 26:</term> mullaikku… ceyti varaku kaḷaikaṭṭalum avai yaṟuttaluṅ kaṭāviṭutalum niraimēyttalum ēṟu kōṭalum</note>
<note xml:lang="ta" target="#atal"><term xml:lang="en">Cf. IAC1, p. 27:</term> marutattukku… ceyti nellaritalum avai kaṭāviṭutalum payirkkuk kaḷaikaṭṭalum</note>
<note xml:lang="ta" target="#kulittal"><term xml:lang="en">Cf. IAC1, p. 25:</term> neytaṟku… ceyti mīṉviṟṟalum uppuviṟṟalum avai paṭuttalum</note> 
</standOff>
<standOff type="notes4" corresp="#TNV9comm3"><note xml:lang="en" target="#inaiyana">This edition follows UVC. The commentary is referring back to the <term xml:lang="ta-Latn"><hi rend="italic">cūttiram</hi></term>, and the <foreign xml:lang="ta-Latn">cūttiram</foreign> reads <q xml:lang="ta-Latn"><hi rend="italic">iṉaiyaṉa</hi></q>.</note>
  <note xml:lang="en" target="#kulittal">As is often the case, it is difficult to disambiguate source and parallel. The IAC provides slightly fuller lists of occupations than this commentary. Much, however, is the same. The relevant passages are quoted in full because, even though there are cases where the treatment is not identical, there are enough similarities to suggest that the IAC was the source.</note>
</standOff>
